#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# range_space

#% text
# `range_space(m)` gives a basis of the span of the columns of the exact matrix `m`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The basis is the nonzero rows of the reduced row echelon form of the transpose of `m`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
range_space([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]])
#% output
#= [[1, 0, -1], [0, 1, 2]]

#% cell
range_space([[3, 1, a], [2, 1, b]])
#% output
#= [[1, 0], [0, 1]]

#% cell
range_space([[1, 2], [2, 4]])
#% output
#= [[1, 2]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `null_space`, `row_reduce`, `rank`
